#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184351 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183947 :question/id #uuid "70fd3433-e905-5643-8e55-0bdf774d781e" :question/math-academy-id "e-14404" :question/problem "Calculate  $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac {e^{2x}} {e^{2x} + 1} \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we introduce the new variable $u = e^{2x}+1.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= 2e^{2x}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\, \\textrm{d}u = e^{2x} \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{e}^{2x}}{{e}^{2x}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{e}^{2x}+1}\\cdot {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{e}^{2x}+1|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2x}+1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we used the fact that $e^{2x} + 1 > 0$ for all $x.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed3b6c3d-b840-50ef-9e6b-584bf14877b3" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049443 :topic/difficulty 1.2233896690425385 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428224 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition uni