{d}u=\\ln\\left|u\\right|+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- 2 x + e^{x} + 3$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(e^{x} - 2)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nUse a connected real interval on which the integrand is defined.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{4 e^{x} - 8}{- 2 x + e^{x} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=4\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n4\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=4\\left(\\ln\\left|u\\right|\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n4\\left(\\ln\\left|- 2 x + e^{x} + 3\\right|\\right)+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679524 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc74a0e7-44e2-5fae-a5db-8d69f134f85d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\left(\\frac{2 \\left(2^{x} + 3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc74a0e7-44e2-5fae-a5db-8d69f134f85d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\left(\\frac{2 \\left(2^{x} + 3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679504} :answer-field/id #uuid "0db88b23-58cf-5ec3-87d8-e693487a62ba" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679428}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fbe42d09-6935-5167-af4a-642732c52ed7" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 2^{x} \\sqrt{2^{x} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\sqrt{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\frac{2 u^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}+C$.\n\nWork where $2^{x} + 3>0$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2^{x} + 3$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(2^{x} \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nWork where $2^{x} + 3>0$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 2^{x} \\sq